<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.niche-hunter.restore-drill</string>

  <!-- Monthly proof that the offsite backup can actually be restored.
       "Recoverable" is production criterion 3, and `nh criteria` reads the log this
       writes: two dated passes AND a newest one inside DRILL_STALE_DAYS. So a schedule
       that dies turns C3 red within 45 days instead of leaving it green forever.

       WHY launchd, when the backup is on cron. The backup writes to iCloud Drive, which
       is TCC-protected, and Full Disk Access is granted per responsible process: cron
       holds it here and a launchd agent does not (measured — see the backup plist's
       header). The --offsite arm has no such problem: it downloads from B2 into a
       mktemp scratch and never touches ~/Library/Mobile Documents. So the constraint
       that pins the backup to cron simply does not apply to this job.

       And for a MONTHLY job, cron is the worse choice. `pmset -g custom` shows
       `sleep 1` on battery: the 09:05 wake, the nightly, and the backup finish around
       09:45, the Mac re-sleeps, and a cron fire after that is silently skipped and never
       retried — the exact mechanism that lost 2026-08-30. launchd replays a
       StartCalendarInterval it slept through, on wake.

       09:55 on the 1st: after the backup window, so the newest object in the bucket is
       whole. A multipart upload in flight is not visible to `s3 ls`, but a partial one
       never is either — the listing only shows completed objects.

       INSTALL:
         cp scripts/launchd/com.niche-hunter.restore-drill.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
         launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.niche-hunter.restore-drill.plist
         launchctl kickstart -p gui/$UID/com.niche-hunter.restore-drill

       That kickstart IS the install verification: it appends a dated pass to
       logs/restore.log, which `nh criteria` then counts. -->

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/mac/Projects/youtube/niche-hunter/scripts/restore_check.sh</string>
    <string>--offsite</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Day</key><integer>1</integer>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>55</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/mac/Projects/youtube/niche-hunter/logs/restore_drill.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/mac/Projects/youtube/niche-hunter/logs/restore_drill.log</string>

  <!-- Never on load: bootstrapping at login must not cost a 266MB download. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
